{"user": "is it better to aim to change white pieces or to protect my own?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T13:51:50.010564+00:00", "assistant": "In the endgame, it\u2019s **not \u201cflip the most now\u201d** \u2014 it\u2019s **finish with the most discs**.\n\nBetter rule of thumb:\n\n- **Corners / stable edge discs** matter most because they can\u2019t be flipped back.\n- Avoid moves that give White an easy **corner** next turn.\n- Think about **mobility**: does your move leave White with few or bad moves?\n- Flipping White pieces is good only if they\u2019re likely to **stay Black** by the end.\n\nFor this position, compare your legal moves by asking: \u201cAfter I play this, what can White do next \u2014 especially near the empty corners/edges?\u201d", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T13:51:56.320520+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T13:51:58.521376+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 2, "Common Ground Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "consensus": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Prompt": 2, "Hint": 2}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Prompt": 0.6666666666666666, "Hint": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle", "Prompt"], "sonnet": ["General Principle", "Hint", "Prompt"], "llama": ["General Principle", "Hint"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used"